    "scope": "For the generic one-integer estimate, ETS7–11 give finiteness and the simultaneous valuation inequalities, with the least possible positive integer for each admissible fixed datum. ETS12–14 prove the stated zero contributions and the bounded-twist, bounded-degree large-prime estimate. Uniform logarithmic size on the full range remains a proof-specific input. The separate source route via a marked ordinary family is examined in ETS3–6."
  },
  "retained_inputs": [
    "For the generic arithmetic count, the product of the eligible primitive parts must satisfy the logarithmic size inequality in PropGK uniformly in the twist, field of the character kernel and level. ETS9–11 give pointwise finiteness, an integer independent of the later coefficient data, its exact minimal valuations, and the local restrictions at every eligible prime. ETS12–14 resolve the stated vanishing and bounded-parameter cases.",
    "On the separate linked-frame proof the ordinary automorphic family must supply its seeds, local Type-I support, exceptional-branch transfers and classicality. The weight-zero finiteness and the two rank conclusions are required at one mark. ETS4–6 check the proposed citation and the support criterion."
  ]
